      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand that you're really pushing yourself here! For muscle soreness, Tylenol (acetaminophen) can help with pain and fever, but it's important to follow the recommended dosage to prevent liver damage – no more than 3,200 milligrams a day for adults. However, since Tylenol might not be giving you the relief you need, consider trying ibuprofen (like Advil or Motrin), Naproxen (Aleve), or a prescription drug like gabapentin or pregabalin for persistent pain, but consult with a healthcare professional before trying any new medication. Remember to always discuss any medication changes with a doctor. Rest is also crucial for recovery, so don't underestimate your body's need to heal. Good luck with your training!",
